---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import { VariantPrism, VariantLanes, VariantFlood, VariantFission } from '../../components/demo/BuildAuraLab.tsx';
---
<Site title="Lab · Build in parallel, in colour" noindex>
  <section class="home-build">
    <h1 class="plan-v-headline">Build in parallel — the wash as the mechanism</h1>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 16px 0 0;">
      Colour is already a state on this site: the Plan section drains a desk as a card leaves it and charges
      the To Do column as one lands. These four make the wash carry the idea instead of sitting behind it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">9a · Prism</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      A graphite beam — the one colourless thing on the stage — hits an edge and refracts into five rays, each
      tinted from a stop of the prism wash. One instruction becomes five branches.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantPrism client:visible />

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">9b · Lanes</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      Five wells filling with the iris wash at their own rates, each with a bloom at its leading edge. The
      Plan section's charge, run five at a time.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantLanes client:visible />

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">9c · Flood</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      The plate opens in graphite with nothing running. Each agent that starts pushes the prism further across
      it, until the whole board is live and the task names sit dark on bright.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantFlood client:visible />

  <section class="home-build" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <h2 class="plan-v-headline">9d · Fission</h2>
    <p style="color: #86868b; max-width: 62ch; margin: 12px 0 0;">
      One white node divides, each split leaving a trail behind it as it travels out to its branch.
    </p>
  </section>
  <VariantFission client:visible />
</Site>
